+++ b/docs/EXTENSION_ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -40,6 +40,24 @@ interface EditorHost {
 
 This contract ensures that extensions integrate seamlessly with tabs, dirty indicators, file watching, and AI edit streaming regardless of the underlying editor technology.
 
+### Native workspace Open
+
+Desktop workspace tab hosts may expose `host.openWorkspaceFile()`. Check that
+method exists before offering the action: embedded, collaborative, virtual and
+older hosts do not provide it. It shows the existing native chooser and returns
+`{status: 'opened', filePath}`, `{status: 'cancelled'}`, or
+`{status: 'refused', reason}`. Open adds or activates a separate tab and retains
+all existing tab contents, including dirty buffers. Selecting an already-open
+file activates that tab without reloading it from disk.
+
+This capability accepts existing workspace text files within the project reader's
+4 MiB limit. The main process applies its existing sender-workspace and symlink
+containment checks; known binary formats, missing files and directories are
+refused. The originating tab must still be active in the same workspace after
+the chooser and file read. `opened` confirms tab state, not a disk save or the
+completion of the destination editor's initialization. Extensions must not call
+Electron IPC or browser file-import APIs to replace this capability.
+
 ### Reporting the current selection to the chat
 
 An editor can tell the AI chat what the user currently has selected. The chat renders each selection as a removable chip above the input, and includes the non-dismissed items' descriptions in the next prompt.
